* FD-04  Input common-mode range ICMR of the amplifier itself
* The inputs sit at V(cms), stepped 0 .. VDD; a DC-only differential servo
* (E sources + L = 1 GH, 1 GF to ground, as in Fig. 7) nulls Vop - Von so the
* amplifier stays open-loop for AC.  At every step: OP, then one AC point at
* {{F_LOW}} Hz with AC 0.5 / 0.5 at 180 degrees in series with the two inputs.
* A symmetric FD amplifier has no CM-to-DM conversion, so ICMR is the range
* where the differential gain stays within 6 dB of its value at VCOM and the
* output common mode stays within 50 mV of VCOM.
{{SEED_OPTION}}
.lib "{{MODEL_LIB}}" {{CORNER}}
{{MC_PARAM}}
.include "{{DUT_FILE}}"
.temp {{TEMP}}
.options reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-15 vntol=1e-9
VDD vdd 0 {{VDD}}
VSS vss 0 0
IBIAS vdd ibias {{IBIAS}}
VCM vcm 0 {{VCM}}
VCMS cms 0 {{VCM}}
EP sp cms outn outp 0.5
EN sn cms outp outn 0.5
LP sp xp 1G
CP xp 0 1G
LN sn xn 1G
CN xn 0 1G
VAP inp xp DC 0 AC 0.5
VAN inn xn DC 0 AC 0.5 180
XDUT vss ibias vdd vcmpin inp inn outp outn {{DUT}}
RVCM_DUT vcm vcmpin 1k
RLP outp vcm {{RL}}
CLP outp 0 {{CL}}
RLN outn vcm {{RL}}
CLN outn 0 {{CL}}
.control
set filetype=ascii
set appendwrite
foreach v {{VCM_LIST}}
  alter vcms dc = $v
  op
  write {{RAW}} v(outp) v(outn) v(cms)
  ac lin 1 {{F_LOW}} {{F_LOW}}
  write {{RAW}} v(outp) v(outn)
end
.endc
.end
